.TH SDL_CPUPauseInstruction 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_CPUPauseInstruction \- A macro to insert a CPU-specific \(dqpause\(dq instruction into the program.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_atomic.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_CPUPauseInstruction() DoACPUPauseInACompilerAndArchitectureSpecificWay
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This can be useful in busy-wait loops, as it serves as a hint to the CPU as to the program\(aqs intent; some CPUs can use this to do more efficient processing\[char46] On some platforms, this doesn\(aqt do anything, so using this macro might just be a harmless no-op\[char46]
.PP
Note that if you are busy-waiting, there are often more-efficient approaches with other synchronization primitives: mutexes, semaphores, condition variables, etc\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This macro is safe to use from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

